MANILA, Philippines — President Ferdinand Marcos Jr. has issued an order establishing the Education Philippines (EduPhil) program to promote the country as a preferred destination for international students seeking higher education, research and training.

Executive Order No. 124 signed Sept. 8 said the Philippine higher education system will strengthen academic cooperation, research collaboration, innovation partnerships and facilitating the entry, stay and education of foreign students.

It establishes an EduPhil Task Force, which shall serve as the principal interagency coordinating body on the promotion, facilitation and development of the program.

